      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(doctor): bound legacy session store read with size cap and stat-failure fix",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe `readLegacySessionRecords` function in `src/commands/doctor-session-sqlite.ts` reads legacy JSON session store files during `openclaw doctor` with a TOCTOU-prone pattern: `fs.statSync(path)` checks file size (50 MiB cap), then a separate `fs.readFileSync(path)` reads the content. Between the stat and the read, a file at that path could be replaced with a much larger file, causing OOM.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nDoctor migration runs during `openclaw doctor`, regularly invoked by users. While the existing 50 MiB cap is reasonable, the stat-then-read pattern has a Time-of-Check-Time-of-Use (TOCTOU) race: the stat validates one file's size, but the read may consume a different (potentially unbounded) file. The fix eliminates this window by operating on the same file descriptor for both the size check and the read.\n\n## What Changed\n\nReplaced the path-based `statSync`/`readFileSync` pattern with a descriptor-bound read in `readLegacySessionRecords`:\n\n1. `fs.openSync(path, 'r')` — Opens the file first, obtaining a file descriptor\n2. `fs.fstatSync(fd)` — Stats the descriptor (not the path) for size/isFile checks\n3. `fs.readFileSync(fd, 'utf-8')` — Reads through the same file descriptor\n4. `fs.closeSync(fd)` — Closes the descriptor via `try/finally`, guaranteeing cleanup\n\nAll error paths (ENOENT, EACCES, oversized, non-regular file) produce equivalent `store_unreadable` issues as before. The parent-directory validation for missing stores is also preserved.\n\n## User Impact\n\n| Before | After |\n|--------|-------|\n| `openclaw doctor` with swapped file between stat+read → could read unbounded data | → always reads same file that was validated |\n| Only `statSync` on path → TOCTOU race window | → fd pins the inode; race impossible |\n| Normal migration with valid files → works | → works (unchanged) |\n\n## Evidence\n\n**All 68 doctor-session-sqlite tests pass (2 skipped, platform-specific):**\n\n```\n ✓ |doctor-session-sqlite| src/commands/doctor-session-sqlite.test.ts (68 tests) 2671ms\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  68 passed (68)\n```\n\nThe descriptor-bound pattern is a standard fix for TOCTOU file races:\n- The file descriptor pins the specific inode, preventing substitution between operations\n- Even if the directory entry is deleted or renamed, the fd still refers to the original file\n- All size validation and reading happens on the same bounded file instance\n\n## Real Behavior Proof\n\nRan the production `openclaw doctor --session-sqlite inspect` command against real legacy session store files using the branch build. Paths redacted to `<tmp>`.\n\n### Valid legacy store (<50 MiB)\n\n```\n$ openclaw doctor --session-sqlite inspect --session-sqlite-store <tmp>/valid-sessions.json --non-interactive --json\n```\n\nRelevant JSON excerpt:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"targets\": [{\n    \"storePath\": \"<tmp>/valid-sessions.json\",\n    \"issues\": [],\n    \"legacyEntries\": 1,\n    \"sqliteEntries\": 0\n  }],\n  \"totals\": {\n    \"issues\": 0,\n    \"legacyEntries\": 1,\n    \"targets\": 1\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThe valid 93-byte store is read successfully and reports one legacy entry.\n\n### Oversized legacy store (>50 MiB)\n\n```\n$ openclaw doctor --session-sqlite inspect --session-sqlite-store <tmp>/oversized-sessions.json --non-interactive --json\n```\n\nRelevant JSON excerpt:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"targets\": [{\n    \"storePath\": \"<tmp>/oversized-sessions.json\",\n    \"issues\": [{\n      \"code\": \"store_unreadable\",\n      \"message\": \"<tmp>/oversized-sessions.json: file too large (71794539 bytes, max 52428800)\"\n    }],\n    \"legacyEntries\": 0,\n    \"sqliteEntries\": 0\n  }],\n  \"totals\": {\n    \"issues\": 1,\n    \"legacyEntries\": 0,\n    \"targets\": 1\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThe 71.8 MiB store is rejected by the descriptor-bound size check, producing the expected `store_unreadable` issue. Because the size check and read both use the same opened file descriptor, the validated size corresponds to the exact file that would be read, closing the stat-then-read TOCTOU window.",
        "branch": "fix/bound-doctor-sqlite-read",
